Chungcheongbuk-do, once a remote agricultural region, has transformed into an advanced industrial hub. However, it sent shockwaves in 2023 by recording the nation&rsquo;s only negative economic growth rate among the 17 metropolitan cities and provinces. The slump in key export industries such as semiconductors and electric vehicles, coupled with youth outmigration and a stagnant domestic market, has shaken its growth engine. Under the slogan &lsquo;Renew Chungbuk! Excite the Residents!&rsquo;, various innovation strategies have been pushed forward under the 8th popularly elected administration, but tangible outcomes are yet to be felt. This report delves into the structural vulnerabilities of Chungbuk&rsquo;s economy and explores practical recovery models.



